🐛 Describe the bug
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/ProcessGroupNCCL.cpp#L2565
for (const auto i : c10::irange(devices.size())) {
    at::cuda::CUDAStream& ncclStream = ncclStreams[i];
    if (!coalescing_state_) {
      (*work->ncclEndEvents_)[i].record(ncclStream);
    }
    work->ncclComms_[i] = ncclComms[i];
  }
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/reducer.cpp#L1605
    bucket.future_work->wait();
    auto future_result = comm_hook_ == nullptr
https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/default_comm_hooks.cpp
c10::intrusive_ptr<c10::ivalue::Future> AllReduceCommHook::runHook(
    GradBucket& bucket) {
  std::vector<at::Tensor> tensors = {bucket.getBufferRef()};
  // Apply the division first to avoid overflow, especially for FP16.
  tensors[0] /= state_->getSize();
  return state_->allreduce(tensors)->getFuture();
}
“bucket.future_work->wait()”  can not  trigger  “(*ncclEndEvents_)[i].block(currentStream),the current stream does not properly wait for a stream executing NCCL. I guess due to the fast execution of NCCL, this error was not triggered.
In addition, then FP16CompressCommHook's then did not wait for allreduce to finish executing, so it immediately executed convert.
